<title>UK: GUS drops as M&amp;S seen in mail order trial.</title>
<headline>GUS drops as M&amp;S seen in mail order trial.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in mail order group Great Universal Stores Plc dipped on Monday as a report in the Times newspaper said Marks &amp; Spencer Plc was preparing to launch trials of a mail order clothes service.</p>
<p>GUS shares were down 3p at 650-1/2 by 0925 GMT in thin volume of 19,975 shares while M&amp;S rose 2-1/2p to 498-1.2.</p>
<p>&quot;The M&amp;S move may give GUS a few worries,&quot; said one dealer, &quot;there is not a huge overlap in what they do but it is enough.&quot;</p>
<p>No-one at M&amp;S was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106 REU</p>
